# Autenticação — /api/accounts/

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api
@password = Tw1st!Senha#Forte

### Cadastro (multipart/form-data; o campo avatar é opcional)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/register/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=TwistBoundary

--TwistBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="username"

twist_demo
--TwistBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="email"

twist_demo@example.com
--TwistBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="password"

{{password}}
--TwistBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="birth_date"

2000-01-15
--TwistBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="first_name"

Twist
--TwistBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="last_name"

Demo
--TwistBoundary--

### Login (identifier aceita e-mail ou username)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "twist_demo",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.access}}
# O refresh token vai num cookie HttpOnly (twist_refresh), mantido pelo cliente HTTP.
# Cookie + header X-Twist-Client: web. Sem cookie jar, envie {"refresh": "..."} no corpo (fallback).

### Renovar o access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/token/refresh/
Content-Type: application/json
X-Twist-Client: web

{}

### Logout (revoga o refresh token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/logout/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Twist-Client: web

{}


### Recuperação de senha — solicita o e-mail (sempre 200, exista ou não a conta)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/password-reset/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "twist_demo@example.com"
}

### Recuperação de senha — confirma (uid e token vêm do link: /redefinir-senha/{uid}/{token})
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/password-reset/confirm/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uid": "COLE_O_UID",
  "token": "COLE_O_TOKEN",
  "new_password": "N0va!Senha#Segura9"
}
